<title>LIECHTENSTEIN: SOCCER-SUBSTITUTE RAZANAUSKAS FLOORS LIECHTENSTEIN.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SUBSTITUTE RAZANAUSKAS FLOORS LIECHTENSTEIN.</headline>
<dateline>VADUZ, Liechtenstein 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liechtenstein's hopes of collecting their first point of their World Cup qualifying campaign were dashed by two goals in the final 25 minutes of their group eight clash against Lithuania.</p>
<p>Second half substitute Tomas Razanauskas broke the deadlock after 65 minutes and Aurelijus Skarbalius added a second in the final minute to give Lithuania a 2-0 win.</p>
<p>Liechtenstien, beaten 11-1 by Macedonia last November, have conceded 31 goals and scored just three in six qualifiers.</p>
</text>
